\unmerge undoes \merge, drawing instruments on their own
staves again.
Its syntax is the following:

\unmerge \inst2

The line above takes \inst2 out of the staff it was merged
to. More than one instrument can be given:

\unmerge \inst2 \inst3

If only one instrument is left on a merged staff, that
staff is no longer merged. Called alone, \unmerge undoes
all merges:

\unmerge

An unknown instrument, or an instrument given more than
once, throws an error.
